WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:02.737
- I got the real clown
here, the queen clown!

00:00:02.737 --> 00:00:03.956
(laughs)
- [Bella] That's right.

00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:08.350
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:09.392
- Hi, everyone!

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:11.679
I'm Bella DeLune and I am a
professional makeup artist.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:13.600
What made me create the clown contouring

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.851
was a collaboration that I did
with another makeup artist.

00:00:16.851 --> 00:00:19.330
Basically, came out with
the idea to respond to

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.463
a lot of the hate that we
were getting on social media.

00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:24.185
I, personally, was called
a clown all the time.

00:00:24.185 --> 00:00:26.644
I said well, I'ma show you
what a real clown looks like.

00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:28.676
I'm able to express myself through makeup.

00:00:28.676 --> 00:00:30.870
Today, I'm gonna be showing you

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.328
the clown contouring on someone else

00:00:33.328 --> 00:00:34.832
and I'm also going to be doing highlight

00:00:34.832 --> 00:00:36.538
and contour on different skin tones

00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:38.123
and we're gonna have fun with it!

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:40.764
- My relationship with
makeup does not exist.

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:42.938
- Makeup terrifies me.

00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:44.116
- I love makeup.

00:00:44.116 --> 00:00:46.595
I just suck at it so badly. (laughs)

00:00:46.595 --> 00:00:48.546
- I've walked into a couple makeup stores,

00:00:48.546 --> 00:00:51.227
I remember in high school,
and that just scared me.

00:00:51.227 --> 00:00:52.934
- I have a vision when I put on makeup

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:55.392
and I want that vision
to actually be realized

00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:57.322
and actually look like
how I see it in my head.

00:00:57.322 --> 00:00:58.968
- I think I'm excited to do something

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.919
totally different than I usually do.

00:01:00.919 --> 00:01:02.219
- This'll be the first time that anyone

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:04.210
will see me with makeup on.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.790
- Turn me into Kim Kardashian! (laughs)

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.632
(upbeat techno music)

00:01:12.835 --> 00:01:14.477
♫ Make the whole party stand up ♫

00:01:14.477 --> 00:01:16.753
- I'm feeling a little Ruby Rose vibe.

00:01:16.753 --> 00:01:19.069
So we're gonna go ahead and do that.

00:01:19.069 --> 00:01:20.613
- I'm glad I can't see the process,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.402
just because, like, when you watch, like,

00:01:22.402 --> 00:01:24.818
YouTube videos or
whatever, they look crazy.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.647
- The BuzzFeed clown contour.

00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:27.947
Face forward, but eyes up.

00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:28.678
- Oh.

00:01:28.678 --> 00:01:29.349
- Yeah, face forward.

00:01:29.349 --> 00:01:30.019
- Face forward.

00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:31.475
- [Bella] Eyes up, yeah.
- [Client] Eyes up.

00:01:31.475 --> 00:01:34.075
- See how it's light,
medium, and then dark

00:01:34.075 --> 00:01:36.818
so when you blend that, it's
actually gonna be much easier.

00:01:36.818 --> 00:01:38.151
The reason why we put all these

00:01:38.151 --> 00:01:40.610
different colors on her
face, some are gonna act

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.042
as blush, some is gonna
act like a color corrector,

00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:47.090
some, obviously, is gonna
highlight and contour the face.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.528
So I'm putting a lightweight foundation.

00:01:49.528 --> 00:01:51.560
What I'm doing is I'm
just color matching you

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.856
and then I'll go in there
with a little bit of highlight

00:01:53.856 --> 00:01:56.375
and then I'll go in with a
little bit of contour as well.

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:58.569
I can't wait to blend everything together!

00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:02.923
(upbeat techno music)

